Bash Notes
Searching in Files
----------------------

grep '^kai' file.txt
 - Matches beginning

grep 'kai$' file.txt
 - Matches end

grep -A1 kai file.txt
 - Find line and print one line after
 - (After. 1 line after)

grep -B1 kai file.txt
 - Find line and print one line before
 - (Before. 1 line before)

grep -C1 kai file.txt
 - Find line and print one line before and one line after
 - (Context. 1 line before and after of context)

grep -i kai file.txt
 - Case insensitive

grep -o '^k.' file.txt
 - Only print the part that matches
 - (Finds what starts with k and ONLY prints k and what comes next(The "." specifies this))

grep -oi '^k.' file.txt
 - Flags can be put together

cat file.txt | grep -i kai | grep ai | grep i
 - Pipes (Pipelines) can be used to grep multiple times

